<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Eohric</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 902</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Eohric was a Danish king of East Anglia, ruling the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vikings">Viking</a> kingdom established by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guthrum">Guthrum</a>. He joined Æthelwold, a rebel cousin of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edward-the-elder">Edward the Elder</a>, in raiding Mercia and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wessex">Wessex</a>, and was killed in the Battle of the Holme around 902, although the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danes">Danes</a> held the field. Little else is recorded of his reign.</p></div>
